A dot operator glued to a numeric literal (`10.AND.`) is lexed as the
operator, not as part of the number, and spaced; operators glued to a
preceding operator (`:=.not.`, `:=-`) get exactly one space
(fmt.operator_spacing issues #83/#88).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Glued;
:PARAMETERS nCount, bReady, bFlag;
:IF nCount>=10.AND.bReady.or.nCount<2.5.AND..not.bFlag;
bFlag:=.not.bFlag;
nCount:=-nCount;
:ENDIF;
:RETURN bFlag;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Glued;
	:PARAMETERS nCount, bReady, bFlag;

	:IF nCount >= 10 .AND. bReady .OR. nCount < 2.5 .AND. .NOT. bFlag;
		bFlag := .NOT. bFlag;
		nCount := -nCount;
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN bFlag;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:5-3:26 warning parenthesize_mixed_logical: '.AND.' binds tighter than '.OR.', so this group is evaluated first - parenthesize it to state the grouping
3:30-3:55 warning parenthesize_mixed_logical: '.AND.' binds tighter than '.OR.', so this group is evaluated first - parenthesize it to state the grouping
